{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HISTORICAL PERFORMANCE CHECK — do not move the blocker to integration. Examined 12 successful GitHub Actions pytest cells across runs 30668764517, 30669480919, and 30670941755 (three Ubuntu Python versions plus macOS). After the 99% progress line, the entire remaining default-suite tail completed in 7.9–34.8s; Linux tails were 17.3–29.5s. Whole default suites completed in 4m18s–6m22s on Linux and 8m21s–14m45s on macOS. The materialization-triggering item was absent from every slowest-25 report, so its phase duration was below each cell cutoff: 2.40–3.61s on Linux and 2.49–4.85s on macOS. Even the slowest listed default-suite phase was only 16.03s Linux / 35.06s macOS. Therefore there is no evidence of normal runtime above one minute; the hours-long behavior is the confirmed per-blob lazy-fetch defect, not legitimate test cost. Moving the item would hide a fast default-suite regression and would not address the mechanism."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785546435148975001,"uuid":"8556863a-baff-458f-bf67-aba74ed40945"}